SUMMARY:2026 CBC Massey Lecture:  Housing Inc.
DESCRIPTION:TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE\nSince 1965\, [CBC IDEAS](http://cbc.ca
 /ideas) has broadcast the Massey Lectures\, exploring the ideas that make 
 us who we are.\n\nWe attend the Massey Lecture every year.\n\n**Housing is
  not a luxury. It is a requirement for human existence.**\n\nIn the 2026 C
 BC Massey Lectures\, **Leilani Farha**\, *global director of The Shift and
  former UN special rapporteur on the Right to Housing*\, reckons with a cr
 isis engineered by governments and perfected by financial firms.\n\nIn her
  first Massey Lecture\, “Home\,” she explores how our homes shape our 
 sense of dignity\, identity\, and security. Because home is so fundamental
  to our lives\, she argues\, our housing system is inextricably linked to 
 the question of who lives\, who dies\, and who counts.\n\n**Ticket link he
 re: ($26-$50) Any seat on any level is a great seat!**\n\nhttps://www.rcmu
 sic.com/concert/the-2026-cbc-massey-lectures-housing-inc-456801\n\nhttps:/
 /ihrp.law.utoronto.ca/ihrp-alumni-spotlight-leilani-farha\n\nhttps://www.c
 bc.ca/radio/ideas/how-to-get-tickets-to-leilani-farhas-cbc-massey-lectures
 -9.7256001
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/toronto-arts-and-culture/events/31589
 1074/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260729T164028Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260729T164028Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
