SUMMARY:AGO Talks: What is Impressionism? ($15)
DESCRIPTION:TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE\nWe'll attend this PANEL talk on ***The
  Impressionist Revolution: Monet to Matisse***\n\nTicket for the **TALK** 
 is $10-$15 (depending on your AGO membership level). If you're **NOT an AG
 O member**\, then gallery admission is extra. FYI.\n\n\\*\\*\\*Join Caro
 line Shields\, Curator\, European Art and Stephan Jost\, Michael and Sonja
  Koerner Director\, and CEO in **conversation about the Impressionis
 t movement**. Take a fresh look at these familiar artists and the style th
 at shocked the world.\n\nSince joining the AGO in 2017\, Caroline Shields 
 has curated the exhibitions *Impressionism in the Age of Industry* (2019) 
 and *Cassatt—McNicoll: Impressionists Between Worlds* (2023).\n\n**Newly
  opened exhibition:**\n\nhttps://ago.ca/exhibitions/impressionist-revoluti
 on-monet-matisse-dallas-museum-art\n\n**Ticket link for the TALK-**-\n\nht
 tps://ago.ca/events/what-impressionism
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/toronto-arts-and-culture/events/31583
 1111/
