SUMMARY:ARC Ensemble:  Artists of the Royal Conservatory ($40)
DESCRIPTION:TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE\nThe **ARC Ensemble** and students of t
 he **Glenn Gould School** explore ***Armenian works composed*** before the
  breakup of the Soviet Union and Armenian independence – captivating and
  evocative music unknown in the West. Included on the program are arrangem
 ents of Armenian folksongs for string quartet\, a compelling Cello Sonata 
 by Avet Terteryan\, and seductive piano miniatures by Alexander Spendiaria
 n and Arno Babadjanian.\n\n**Ticket link is below**\\-\\-\\-and\\-\\-\\-AN
 Y seat is a great seat\\.\n\nhttps://bit.ly/ARCConcertOct4\n\nThe multiple
  Grammy Award nominated ARC Ensemble comprises the senior faculty of The R
 oyal Conservatory's Glenn Gould School\, with special guests drawn from th
 e organization's most accomplished students and alumni. **It is among Cana
 da's most distinguished cultural ambassadors** with recent appearances in 
 Los Angeles\, New York and London’s Wigmore Hall. The research and recov
 ery of music suppressed and marginalized under the 20th century's repressi
 ve regimes remains its focus and a growing number of works have now rejoin
 ed the repertoire.\n“As always with this ensemble\, performances could h
 ardly be bettered in terms of execution and commitment.” (*Gramophone*)\
 n\n**ARC Ensemble-**\n**(Artists of The Royal Conservatory)**\n\n**Erika R
 aum**\, violin\n**Marie Bérard**\, violin\n**Steven Dann**\, viola\n**Tho
 mas Wiebe**\, cello\n**Kevin Ahfat**\, piano\n\nwith students of **The Gle
 nn Gould School-**\n\n**Avery Tracy**\, violin\n**Gina Lanzrein**\, violin
 \n**Shyler Macaggi**\, viola\n**Mira Kardan**\, cello\n\n**TICKET Link her
 e:**\n\nhttps://www.rcmusic.com/concert/arc-ensemble-453001?utm_source=mee
 tup&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=453001_ARCconcert&utm_content=arts_ev
 ents_listing
